---
// Performance measures — a Workspace settings section (Settings › Projects).
// The tenant's measure catalog, one table; each measure opens on its own
// page, as every settings record does (the side sheet went 2026-10-08). Moved out of the app rail's More on 2026-10-08: setting measures up
// is administration, and a measure's results are read on projects and
// classifications, not here.
//
// SUBCATEGORY SCHEMAS ARE HIDDEN (2026-10-02): not planned for use, so the
// Schemas view, its sheet and the table's Subcategory schemas column are off
// this page. firma2-schema-table / firma2-schema-sidesheet stay in the repo.
//
// The brief's five (docs/product-brief.md §5):
//
// 1. ONE QUESTION: "What does this program measure, and is each measure ready
//    to collect?"
// 2. READERS: program admins configure; the client decision-maker reads the
//    catalog cold. Hardest to serve: the admin's ABSENT counterpart — the
//    REPORTER, who meets every measure configured here as a form they fill.
// 3. SERIES/SCALAR: one homogeneous list — a table, not a rail. Nothing
//    scalar leads.
// 4. IRREVERSIBLE: nothing is (drafts are browser-local patches), so nothing
//    gets a warning band.
// 5. CUT: editing in the grid and in a side sheet over it — a measure is
//    edited on its own page (performance-measures/[measure]). Also cut: the
//    concept library dialog.
//
// SETUP IS STILL NOT A WIZARD (§4): the measure's page saves a Draft in any
// state of completeness, and Active is gated — not the form. The type fork is
// a field like any other, changeable until publishing makes it consequential.
//
// The app chrome and the page's padding come from AppLayout → esa-app-shell.
// The page is its manifest: a header and the measure table.
import AppLayout from '../../../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import EsaButton from '@esa/ecology/esa-button.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../../lib/base';
import Firma2PageHeader from '../../../components/shared/firma2-page-header.astro';
import Firma2MeasureTable from '../../../components/measures/firma2-measure-table.astro';
---
<!-- manifest:
  layout: stack(2xl)
  sections:
    - page header      -> firma2-page-header
    - measures         -> firma2-measure-table
-->
<AppLayout title="Performance measures — Workspace settings — ProjectFirma 2.0" nav="workspace-settings" active="ws-performance-measures">
  <div class="stack" data-gap="2xl">
    <Firma2PageHeader title="Performance measures" aliasableTitle>
      <!-- Straight to the add page, like every settings list: it already
           offers both ways in (a claim, or two questions) and a blank one. -->
      <EsaButton slot="actions" variant="primary" icon="plus" tag="a" href={withBase('/prototypes/workspace-settings/performance-measures/new')}>New measure</EsaButton>
    </Firma2PageHeader>

    <Firma2MeasureTable />
  </div>
</AppLayout>

